1
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:15,999
[Music] Thank You, Jesus. Praise You, Jesus. Glory to You, Jesus. Worship to You, Jesus. On this most holy altar,

2
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:22,999
I thank the Holy Mother and the Holy Child countless times for allowing me and my husband to give this testimony.

3
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:30,999
My name is Soumya Manoj, and I am from Pathanamthitta. I first took the online covenant in

4
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:37,999
15/08/2022. Later, since I was abroad, my husband came here and

5
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:45,999
took the pilgrimage covenant in 22/08/2022. From then on, both of us have been living the covenant life.

6
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:52,999
In 15/08,/2023 I came back to India and took the pilgrimage covenant myself.

7
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:59,999
During our covenant journey, we received a miraculous healing, which I am sharing for the first time.

8
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:06,999
My husband has diabetes. It had only been two months since he started taking medication.

9
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:11,999
But he developed a condition that often affects people who have been on long-term medication—it's called cellulitis.

10
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:18,999
This happened in 2024. Suddenly, his leg started swelling and turning red, and we...

11
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:23,999
We consulted a doctor, and after checking, he said that a week's rest and some antibiotics would be enough.

12
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:29,999
But by the third day, his leg had already started swelling badly. The night I noticed the swelling—I wasn’t even in India then.

13
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:34,999
I was at my workplace in the Gulf. Suddenly, a strong thought came to me: “He needs to go to Kottayam Medical College immediately.”

14
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:41,999
That very night, my husband drove himself to the Medical College. Meanwhile, my mother came from home—

15
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:46,999
to the hospital. As soon as the doctors saw his leg,

16
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:51,999
they asked, “Did you drive yourself here?” They immediately admitted him and asked him to lie down.

17
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:57,999
After my mother reached, the doctors confirmed it was cellulitis—an infection that had started to spread upwards internally.

18
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:04,999
They said that if it worsens, they might have to cut open the lower part of the leg and remove the infected flesh. They said,

19
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:11,999
“We’ll try our best to avoid that, but you must pray.” So, my mother signed the consent form. It was 12 midnight there.

20
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:17,999
For me, at my workplace, it was 9:30 PM. When I saw the condition of his leg, I fell on my knees and reminded myself: “I am in covenant life.”

21
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:25,999
I cried out in prayer to Mother Mary: “Mother, give us the strength to endure this situation.

22
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:34,999
They took my husband to the theatre. The infection was near a main artery, so they gave him local anesthesia. Then, they made

23
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:41,999
deep incisions on both sides of the leg, cutting all the way to the bone. That entire procedure took one and a half hours.

24
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:48,999
And throughout that one and a half hours, I remained on my knees, praying. I offered up a money covenant on behalf of my husband.

25
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:55,999
He was in severe pain after the surgery, but not even once did he call out in complaint. I believe he united his suffering with that of Jesus.

26
00:02:56,000 --> 00:03:01,999
My husband lay there praying, “Lord, give me the strength to endure this pain.” He recited the Creed while lying down.

27
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:07,999
The doctors then told us, “We haven’t removed any flesh—we only made deep incisions. But now,

28
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:13,999
he must be admitted to a smaller hospital where they can manage it using an aseptic technique. The wound has to be cared for

29
00:03:14,000 --> 00:03:20,999
with utmost cleanliness, and daily dressings are required.” So we went to a nearby local hospital and got admitted.

30
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:26,999
That same day, they dressed the wound. The sisters at the hospital were shocked.

31
00:03:27,000 --> 00:03:32,999
They wondered, “Why did they go to a medical college for this and come back with such heavy bandaging?”

32
00:03:33,000 --> 00:03:40,999
The next morning, they asked my husband to walk to the dressing room. The day after, they had to wash the wound with soap.

33
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:46,999
As soon as the wound was opened, four nurses came running from all sides—they didn’t know what to do.

34
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:52,999
They had never seen a wound like that before. Even after using all the dressing materials in their room, it wasn’t enough.

35
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:58,999
And so began one and a half months of daily dressings at that hospital.

36
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:04,999
Despite the unbearable pain, my husband never once missed the apparition prayers. Neither did I.

37
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:09,999
He would stand on that very leg and pray aloud. Mother Mary gave us that strength.

38
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:16,999
It took four full months, but his leg completely healed. We thank Jesus and Mother Mary endlessly.

39
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:21,999
The doctors had said that part of the leg might need to be removed. And my husband is a driver—

40
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:27,999
our only source of income is through his driving. We were afraid—would he ever drive again?

41
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:31,999
After we began faithfully living the covenant,

42
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:39,999
he hasn't had to take any medication at all. As for me, for the past 23 years, I had irregular periods.

43
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:43,999
Sometimes it would take two or three months to come, sometimes it wouldn’t come at all.

44
00:04:44,000 --> 00:04:49,999
I used to take medication, stop for a while, and start again. But when I entered covenant life, I didn’t even pray specifically for it.

45
00:04:50,000 --> 00:04:55,999
Yet, from then until this very moment—on the 28th day, every month, my cycle has been perfectly regular. That’s a great blessing.

46
00:04:56,000 --> 00:05:04,999
And not just that. In 2021, we had a child—after 11 years of marriage.

47
00:05:05,000 --> 00:05:12,999
Two years after our wedding, I became pregnant, but it ended in a miscarriage. In 2020, I conceived again.

48
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:18,999
In March 2021, my water broke at six and a half months. I was admitted to the hospital and gave birth.

49
00:05:19,000 --> 00:05:25,999
The baby was admitted to Kottayam Medical College. On the 23rd day, the baby aspirated milk during feeding.

50
00:05:26,000 --> 00:05:27,999
The sisters were feeding him, but they didn’t take care properly,

51
00:05:28,000 --> 00:05:35,999
and he died in my arms. After that, I developed piles. I completely broke down—I felt like I had gone mad.

52
00:05:36,000 --> 00:05:42,999
For 23 days I had been breastfeeding, and suddenly my breasts got infected—

53
00:05:43,000 --> 00:05:50,999
they became swollen and developed abscesses three times. I couldn’t even take any medicine because of the piles.

54
00:05:51,000 --> 00:05:58,999
After two months, a friend told me, “You’ll go crazy if you continue like this. You should go back to work.”

55
00:05:59,000 --> 00:06:04,999
So my friend Shaija from Bombay booked me a flight and took me there.

56
00:06:05,000 --> 00:06:10,999
She took care of me for two months. After that, I worked in Bombay for just two months,

57
00:06:11,000 --> 00:06:16,999
and then got an opportunity to go abroad. So I went to the Gulf.

58
00:06:17,000 --> 00:06:23,999
If I had to describe my life before coming to Kreupasanam, Father would say, “Zero minus zero.”

59
00:06:24,000 --> 00:06:29,999
And if there’s anything lower than that, that was my situation. I only had debts to speak of.

60
00:06:30,000 --> 00:06:34,999
Though I was earning nearly one lakh rupees in salary, I didn’t know what to do with it.

61
00:06:35,000 --> 00:06:41,999
I had to pay off people. By the time the salary came and went, we were left with nothing.

62
00:06:42,000 --> 00:06:47,999
No house, no land, no child—only emptiness. But I had no complaint. I believed,

63
00:06:48,000 --> 00:06:53,999
“Whatever God has planned for me, He will give. That’s enough.” I continued working.

64
00:06:54,000 --> 00:06:59,999
When I came to Kreupasanam, I prayed to Mother Mary: “Mother, I don’t know what my life is. Please organize it.”

65
00:07:00,000 --> 00:07:04,999
“I don’t even know where to begin,” I said. I prayed. The rest of the intentions were for others,

66
00:07:05,000 --> 00:07:09,999
but they’re not with me now, so I won’t share them.

67
00:07:10,000 --> 00:07:18,999
In 2022 itself, during my husband’s first covenant period, we got a chance to buy a piece of land.

68
00:07:19,000 --> 00:07:27,999
We made an agreement by paying just ₹25,000. But we needed ₹9 lakh to complete the payment.

69
00:07:28,000 --> 00:07:33,999
We had no money. The notice period was six months. We didn’t know how we’d raise the money.

70
00:07:34,000 --> 00:07:38,999
So I started praying to Mother Mary. I would say the rosary every day. I offered perpetual rosary.

71
00:07:39,000 --> 00:07:43,999
My husband didn’t know anything about rosaries or how to pray. We are from a Hindu background.

72
00:07:44,000 --> 00:07:48,999
He watched videos on YouTube, wrote down the prayers, and learned how to pray each part.

73
00:07:49,000 --> 00:07:55,999
He prayed, and I prayed. Even before signing the agreement for the property,

74
00:07:56,000 --> 00:08:00,999
we had gone there to look at a five-cent plot. I prayed to Mother Mary and said,

75
00:08:01,000 --> 00:08:05,999
“Mother, we don’t have money to give any brokers. You yourself must stand as the mediator for this.”

76
00:08:06,000 --> 00:08:10,999
Then, someone directly told us, “I know a place nearby. If you go and ask personally, it might work out.”

77
00:08:11,000 --> 00:08:16,999
So my husband went to ask. At that moment, I told Mother Mary,

78
00:08:17,000 --> 00:08:22,999
“As he goes, I will stay back and pray. I’ll light candles here. For every step he takes, I’ll offer a prayer.”

79
00:08:23,000 --> 00:08:26,999
I lit two candles and prayed deeply for that intention. I told Mother,

80
00:08:27,000 --> 00:08:32,999
“Mother, it’s just five cents of land. Today, even to dig a well, it takes a lot of money.

81
00:08:33,000 --> 00:08:38,999
And there’s not even space to dig a well.” Just two minutes after I said that, my husband told me,

82
00:08:39,000 --> 00:08:44,999
“Hey, there’s already a well on that land. If we buy the plot, they will give us the well too.”

83
00:08:45,000 --> 00:08:49,999
That’s when I realized—Mother Mary had gifted us the well. For almost 40 years,

84
00:08:50,000 --> 00:08:54,999
that well had provided water to all the people living in that area. We signed the agreement. But within 6 months,

85
00:08:55,000 --> 00:09:01,999
we had to settle the full payment. We didn’t have the money. Again, we prayed, asking Mother how this would be possible.

86
00:09:02,000 --> 00:09:06,999
We had taken the agreement before the Rosary Rally. We prayed to finish it in time.

87
00:09:07,000 --> 00:09:12,999
We had two chitty (community saving schemes), both were stuck for a long time.

88
00:09:13,000 --> 00:09:17,999
Around 20 installments were overdue, but somehow, both chitties were closed—

89
00:09:18,000 --> 00:09:24,999
we paid off all pending installments. Then, both chitty amounts—about ₹2 lakhs—were given to us one month after the other.

90
00:09:25,000 --> 00:09:30,999
We arranged the rest of the money from well-wishers and finished the property agreement just before the Rosary Rally.

91
00:09:31,000 --> 00:09:36,999
We had made a decision: We won't make personal intentions or prayer petitions anymore. We’d leave it to Mother and Jesus.

92
00:09:37,000 --> 00:09:43,999
So after that, we didn’t have any prayer requests of our own. We prayed for others. Their pain became our pain.

93
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:47,999
So when my husband asked, “Why aren’t you making any intentions anymore?” I replied,

94
00:09:48,000 --> 00:09:51,999
“Isn’t that something we’ve already handed over to God? He knows everything.”

95
00:09:52,000 --> 00:09:54,999
But yes, the only thing we now hoped for was a house.

96
00:09:55,000 --> 00:09:58,999
My husband participated in the Rosary Rally. During that time,

97
00:09:59,000 --> 00:10:03,999
I stayed back and recited the Rosary for five hours. After that year’s Rosary Rally ended,

98
00:10:04,000 --> 00:10:14,999
we continued our covenant life. But we didn’t pray for a house very immediately.

99
00:10:15,000 --> 00:10:21,999
Because that was the time of the floods. Many people, even those who had beautiful houses, became homeless,

100
00:10:22,000 --> 00:10:23,999
especially in Wayanad.

101
00:10:24,000 --> 00:10:26,999
So we didn’t see our situation as a big problem.

102
00:10:27,000 --> 00:10:30,999
We just kept praying, “Let Your will be done, Jesus and Mother Mary.”

103
00:10:31,000 --> 00:10:39,999
And before the 2024 Rosary Rally, our house construction structure was completed.

104
00:10:40,000 --> 00:10:45,999
My husband brought our priest to see the plan. We planned a two-story house.

105
00:10:46,000 --> 00:10:52,999
But at that time, my husband’s leg condition worsened and my mother fell seriously ill—liver cirrhosis.

106
00:10:53,000 --> 00:10:58,999
We didn’t even know she was that sick. My husband was admitted to the hospital, and my mother stayed at home with him.

107
00:10:59,000 --> 00:11:03,999
My sister-in-law, who had two small children, cooked three meals a day, washed his clothes—

108
00:11:04,000 --> 00:11:08,999
she took care of everything. We couldn’t take my mother to the hospital. When my husband left,

109
00:11:09,000 --> 00:11:17,999
she was perfectly fine. But then she deteriorated quickly. We had to take her to Kottayam Medical College.

110
00:11:18,000 --> 00:11:20,999
She was admitted for five days. They said it was end-stage liver cirrhosis and nothing more could be done.

111
00:11:21,000 --> 00:11:28,999
Our house had a small toilet located around 50 meters away. At that time, I was the only one earning.

112
00:11:29,000 --> 00:11:33,999
So I couldn't stay with her full-time. We arranged for someone else to care for her.

113
00:11:34,000 --> 00:11:40,999
But by the last 15 days, her hands and legs stopped moving. She became fully bedridden.

114
00:11:41,000 --> 00:11:50,999
My husband couldn’t walk. I couldn’t travel. I had taken advance salary just to handle these emergencies.

115
00:11:51,000 --> 00:11:57,999
We prayed to Jesus and Mother Mary. Even if we asked for food or cleaning support,

116
00:11:58,000 --> 00:12:03,999
they could only help when they had resources. We prayed,

117
00:12:04,000 --> 00:12:08,999
“If there's no way out, please show mercy, Jesus and Mother Mary.”

118
00:12:09,000 --> 00:12:14,999
Honestly, I couldn’t fulfill my duties to my mother fully.

119
00:12:15,000 --> 00:12:21,999
When we talk about doing mission or charity work—what’s the point if we can’t do our duty to our own mother?

120
00:12:22,000 --> 00:12:27,999
We had no one else to help us. We looked for rental homes so we could take her and care for her,

121
00:12:28,000 --> 00:12:36,999
but no one would rent to someone with a bedridden patient. They feared someone might die there.

122
00:12:37,000 --> 00:12:41,999
So I prayed, “Mother, please give us a single room, a toilet, and a small kitchen.”

123
00:12:42,000 --> 00:12:46,999
I made that prayer with all my heart. But within 15 days, my mother passed away.

124
00:12:47,000 --> 00:12:55,999
I couldn’t return. I had used all my advance salary. But I handled everything—her care, her final sacrements.

125
00:12:56,000 --> 00:13:01,999
Just 16 days after that, we were able to start house construction. In just one month,

126
00:13:02,000 --> 00:13:07,999
we completed the structure. Then our funds ran out. We waited and prayed patiently for five months.

127
00:13:08,000 --> 00:13:14,999
I had planned to come in May. I prayed, “Mother, before I return in May, please finish the work—

128
00:13:15,000 --> 00:13:20,999
even if it’s just one room ready, I’ll be happy.”

129
00:13:21,000 --> 00:13:25,999
We had made one request: if the house was completed before we came,

130
00:13:26,000 --> 00:13:30,999
we would receive the key and only then move in.

131
00:13:31,000 --> 00:13:36,999
We had no idea how, but everything got done. It’s a small, humble house,

132
00:13:37,000 --> 00:13:40,999
and we named it Kripabhavan—a heavenly home.

133
00:13:41,000 --> 00:13:45,999
We have only one photo in the house—Mother Mary’s. People ask, “You’re Hindus, why is her photo here?”

134
00:13:46,000 --> 00:13:50,999
And I say, “Because it’s her house. She gave it to us.”

135
00:13:51,000 --> 00:13:57,999
On the 16th, we moved in. But right after that, my husband had an accident.

136
00:13:58,000 --> 00:14:04,999
There was no water in the tank. He climbed up to fix it, took a pipe from the neighbor's line—

137
00:14:05,000 --> 00:14:11,999
and while coming down, a wooden piece used to hold the pipe fell on his head.

138
00:14:12,000 --> 00:14:18,999
Blood started pouring. At first, he felt fine, and we went to a nearby clinic. They said it was nothing.

139
00:14:19,000 --> 00:14:23,999
But after coming home, bleeding started again. I couldn’t even change clothes. I was trembling.

140
00:14:24,000 --> 00:14:28,999
I said, “Mother, we’re going to Kottayam Medical College. Please come with us.”

141
00:14:29,000 --> 00:14:38,999
We got a CT scan done there. I said, “Mother, let the scan be normal. I’ll come Thursday to thank You.”

142
00:14:39,000 --> 00:14:43,999
We waited for the result—it was normal.

143
00:14:44,000 --> 00:14:49,999
There was no fracture, no danger. Just minor treatment was needed.

144
00:14:50,000 --> 00:14:54,999
By 5 PM, the results came and everything was fine.

145
00:14:55,000 --> 00:14:59,999
That’s how many, many times during our covenant life, Jesus and Mother Mary have protected us.

146
00:15:00,000 --> 00:15:04,999
Once, while riding a two-wheeler, a car suddenly came from a side road and hit us.

147
00:15:05,000 --> 00:15:09,999
We fell onto a divider. But nothing happened to us—only minor damage to the vehicle.

148
00:15:10,000 --> 00:15:12,999
That’s how God saves us again and again.

149
00:15:13,000 --> 00:15:18,999
The covenant is truly a blessing that protects us—this is something I can strongly affirm through my own testimony.

150
00:15:19,000 --> 00:15:22,999
I give endless thanks to Mother Mary and to Jesus for showering us with so many blessings.

151
00:15:23,000 --> 00:15:29,999
Now, our Karthavinte Perunnal (Feast of the Lord) was set for June 16.

152
00:15:30,000 --> 00:15:33,999
But June 15 was a day of heavy rain—literally 24 hours of nonstop downpour.

153
00:15:34,000 --> 00:15:40,999
So, the next morning, my husband and I lit two candles and offered a prayer of presence.

154
00:15:41,000 --> 00:15:46,999
Then we went around our house, praying the Creed, and I told Mother Mary: “Mother, based on our invitation, many people are coming from different places today.

155
00:15:47,000 --> 00:15:52,999
They have to return safely after the gathering. So please, don’t let it rain today.

156
00:15:53,000 --> 00:15:58,999
I asked Mother for a sign that this would be granted.”

157
00:15:59,000 --> 00:16:10,999
And what a miracle! During the milk boiling ceremony for the feast, there was only a 2-second drizzle—

158
00:16:11,000 --> 00:16:15,999
other than that, no rain at all that day. Such a blessing for us!

159
00:16:16,000 --> 00:16:20,999
Now about our daily evangelization life: I can't do much physically because I’m not there in person. But I pray many rosaries every day.

160
00:16:21,000 --> 00:16:26,999
I offer intentions for others, give financial offerings, and my husband provides food to orphanages.

161
00:16:27,000 --> 00:16:33,999
We also help people we meet on the roadside—especially the sick. Even those with conditions we’ve never heard of—we try to help with treatment.

162
00:16:34,000 --> 00:16:39,999
If we can feed even one person a day, we do it.

163
00:16:40,000 --> 00:16:48,999
One transformation after entering into the covenant is this divine experience: We no longer hold grudges or argue with anyone.

164
00:16:49,000 --> 00:16:53,999
Even those who wrong us—we now pray for them with a forgiving heart.

165
00:16:54,000 --> 00:16:57,999
When we see others in pain, we feel that pain as our own and pray deeply for them.

166
00:16:58,000 --> 00:17:03,999
Jesus and Mother Mary have truly blessed us with this heart. We are eternally grateful for these blessings.

167
00:17:04,000 --> 00:17:12,999
Philippians 1:29 says, “For it has been granted to you on behalf of Christ not only to believe in him, but also to suffer for him.”

168
00:17:13,000 --> 00:17:19,999
As Soumi Chechi (Sister) said—she prays the rosary for five hours or more every day,

169
00:17:20,000 --> 00:17:26,999
recites the uninterrupted rosary, kneels in prayer, and intercedes for others— this grace to endure and offer suffering has also been given to us.

170
00:17:27,000 --> 00:17:31,999
Because through this covenant, we have come to truly understand Christ.

171
00:17:32,000 --> 00:17:40,999
Even during difficult times—like when my husband's leg condition became serious—Christ stood with us.

172
00:17:41,000 --> 00:17:47,999
Mother Mary helped our family through the covenant.

173
00:17:48,000 --> 00:17:54,999
That’s why we’re now willing to be witnesses— even willing to suffer for Christ. Through Mother Mary, God has blessed us so much.

174
00:17:55,000 --> 00:18:00,999
Let us clap our hands and glorify God for these blessings! Jesus, thank You. Jesus, we praise You. Jesus, we adore You.

175
00:18:01,000 --> 00:18:09,999
These divine experiences can happen to you too. If you haven’t subscribed to our YouTube channel yet—

176
00:18:10,000 --> 00:18:16,999
please do so now. Share this video with your friends,

177
00:18:17,000 --> 00:18:21,000
and become an instrument in the hands of the Lord.
